a }_{1}=-3,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=8.$ So, the third column of $P$ corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{3}=8.$ \n\nNow, we need to find an eigenvector that corresponds to ${\\lambda }_{3}=8.$ Computing $A-8I,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-8I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]-8[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-8I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector \n\n$$\n{v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $‖{v}_{3}‖=\\sqrt{22}.$ Dividing ${v}_{3}$ by its norm, we obtain the third column of $P:$ \n\n$$\n\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{22}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505873 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505873 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7093551b-07fc-5ff1-a4c8-030bdccede09" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505873 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186357709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505878 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505878 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7f92a652-43f6-587a-a8b8-f62ae03dfd9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505878 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186404693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505879 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505879 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95bdc2bb-7bd0-5a10-b18b-ed936f4da1af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505879 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186505739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505888 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186505879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c90bbda8-2d90-5c6d-95b2-4a5ad309bb13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186505888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186505766